.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt SYSADMINCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysadminctl
.Nd establish the first owner of an rmxOS installation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl addUser Ar user
.Fl hostName Ar hostname
.Fl sshPublicKey Ar file
.Op Fl altRoot Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs as root and applies owner state once, using the same writer as
.Xr rmxos-install 8 .
.Fl addUser
uses the macOS command's terminology; the other switches are rmxOS additions.
The default root is the running system, otherwise
.Fl altRoot
names an installed root with its Data datasets mounted.
All three values are required and use the installer's hostname,
lowercase user name (excluding root and toor), and single OpenSSH
public-key-line validators.
They are checked before any write.
.Pp
The command adds a user with no password, a home at
.Pa /Users/ Ns Ar user
(mode 0755),
.Pa .ssh
(0700) and
.Pa authorized_keys
(0600), owned by that user's uid and gid.
It locks root, rebuilds the password databases, sets the hostname,
loads mac_do on subsequent boots and writes the user's mdo rule.
It does not ask for or set a user password.
Before an owner is added, the template's empty root password permits
console access only; sshd refuses root and empty-password logins.
.Pp
Completion is recorded in
.Pa /private/var/db/rmxos/owner .
That marker, an existing security.mac.do.rules setting, or a root
password beginning with *LOCKED* indicates an owner, including installations
made by the earlier installer.
Such roots are refused without changing any files.
An existing account with the requested name is also refused.
The existing etc directory is locked to serialize owner writers without
creating a lock file during a refusal.
Operational errors after account creation can leave partial owner state;
inspect it before retrying.
This command does not replace or remove owners.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rmxos-install 8 ,
.Xr rmxos-owner-seed 8
